window.docContents[157].resolve({"/#Graph-Theory-in-Lean":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"","header":"Graph Theory in Lean","id":"/#Graph-Theory-in-Lean"},"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity":{"contents":"* isoSigmaConnectedComponents: the isomorphism between G and the sigma graph of\nits connected components.* EdgesInOneComponent: every edge of G lies in a single connected component (any\ntwo non-isolated vertices are reachable from each other).* locallyFiniteDeleteEdges: the graph G.deleteEdges s obtained by deleting\nedges from a locally finite graph is locally finite.* IsVertexConnected: predicate for a graph being k-vertex-connected\n(k : ℕ∞, as for Mathlib's IsEdgeConnected).* edgeConnectivity / λ(G): the edge connectivity\nλ(G) : ℕ∞, the supremum of the k for which G is\nk-edge-connected.* vertexConnectivity / κ(G): the vertex connectivity\nκ(G) : ℕ∞, the supremum of the k for which G is\nk-vertex-connected.* walkComponent: the set of vertices of a finite set W reachable from v₂ by a\nwalk lying inside W.* IsCutVertex: x is a cut vertex of G (some two vertices other than x are\njoined by a walk, but every walk between them passes through x).* CycleEquivalent: two edges are cycle-equivalent if they are equal or lie on a\ncommon cycle.* BlockEquivalent: the equivalence relation on edges generated by\nCycleEquivalent.* blockSetoid: the setoid instance on G.edgeSet given by block-equivalence.* Block: a block of G, i.e. a block-equivalence class of edges.* blockMk: the block containing a given edge.* Adj.block: the block containing the edge u — v, written h.block for\nh : G.Adj u v.* Block.toSubgraph: the subgraph of G underlying a block, formed by the edges of\nG in that block and their endpoints.* Block.map: the image of a block under a copy f : Copy G G', the block\ncontaining the images of its edges.* Subgraph.homOfMapLE: a homomorphism f restricts to a homomorphism\nH.coe →g H'.coe whenever H.map f ≤ H'.* SplitsAt: G is the union of two proper subgraphs whose supports meet in at most\na given vertex.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* botComponentEquiv: equivalence between the connected components of the empty\ngraph and its vertex type.* Hom.sigmaDesc: the universal property of the disjoint union: a family of\nhomomorphisms G i →g H gives a homomorphism Σg G →g H.* Finset.fiberProj: the vertices z of G whose copy (z, b) in the G-fibre at\nb of G □ K₂ lies in a given vertex set.* bowtie: two triangles sharing a vertex, a graph with κ(G) < λ(G).* barbell: two copies of K[4] joined by an edge, a graph with λ(G) < δ(G).\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Definitions","header":"14.2.9. Chapter 10: Connectivity","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity"}});